#1100
The Western Entrance~
   At the western side of a small man-made cave you take a minute to look
around.  The cave entrance itself is made of five or six gigantic slabs, at the
time the stone they were made of was a beautiful white color, or so you
imagine, because now the slabs have deteriorated and changed to a brownish
color.  As noticed before, this is the western half of the entrance, it is
actually one large entrance that has just been divided by a large slab of the
same stone used on the outer walls.  Looking into the entrance, it's pretty
dark, and all you can see is a few steps decending into the cave.  As you take
your gaze away from the entrance, you see the steps going down the hill, and a
small semi-trail going east to the other side of the entrance.    
~
11 4 3
D0
~
~
0 0 1129
D1
