~
0 0 1101
D5
~
~
0 0 1103
E
entrance~
   Looking closely at the entrance itself yields very little new information
not already noticed by looking from a distance.  You can tell though that the
stone that the entrance is made if is some pretty old stuff.  In some of the
recently chipped or cracked areas you can see the original white color of the
rock, but it has since turned a light brown.  Using your best judgement, the
slabs are about two feet wide, thick enough to withstand time for a very long
time, and even though you can see the rock slowy deteriorating, you figure that
it will still last a long time.    
~
S
#1101
The Eastern Entrance~
   The eastern half of the entrance is a fairly calm place actually, you don't
seem to see anything out of the ordinary.  Looking at the entrance itself you
see that it is made of several large slabs of a faded white stone, and has been
divided by one very t square slab of stone in the center.  Not quite
understanding why the entrance is divided you simply shrug and continue looking
around, you notice that there is a large amount of moss growing on and in the
stone slabs that make up the entrance.  The large entrance itself is a huge
square that holds steps decending deep into the ground, a man-made cave of some
sort.  Looking around you decide you need to make a choice, you can go north
into the entrance, down the steps that lead to the bottom of the hill, or you
could go to the west along a small semi-trail to the other entrance.    
~
