#1103
The Steps~
   On the ground here, large rocks protrude out of the small hill you are on,
forming large natural steps that lead to and from a large cave entrance and a
small unused dirt trail.  The rocks that make up these natural steps are some
unknown stone, but appear to be very sturdy and you do not think you should
have any problem walking on them.  As you look around you get a strange
feeling, wondering who created this cave, exactly why they made it, and how
these rocks being here is just a little too convenient.  The steps go north and
south, north to a cave entrance, and south to a small unused dirt trail, but
they are also directly connected with another set to the east.    
~
