#1105
A Small Trail~
   The ground here is made of dirt, and is void of all plantlife though moss
and small clumps of grass grow about six inches out from the center,
effectively making this some sort of walking trail.  Making a tight circle
around the base of a small hill here, the trail is mainly useless, but by
walking on it you could get a good look at things.  Taking a close look at the
trail you can barely see the tops of large stepping stones that have been
buried here to make the trail.  Bringing your gaze up from the ground you are
puzzled by this whole thing, out here in the middle of nowhere.  To the north
this small trail goes up to some steps leading up the hill, but it also travels
around the hill to both the east and west.  The clearing extends also extends
to the south a small bit, but no trail goes in that direction.    
~
