#1106
A Southeastern Bend in the Trail~
   The trail you are on curves here making a sort of corner while still
traveling tight at the base of a small hill.  This trail appears to have never
been used before, though is just as bare as a dirt trail or road that is
heavily used.  Lightly covered by dirt, you see the tops of large stepping
stones buried under the trail to make walking easier.  You have no idea who put
this trail here, or why they did it, but you really don't give it much thought.
The trail itself continues around the hill both north and west, but the
clearing extends further out to the east, where you see a large monument or
statue of some sort.    
~
