0 0 1106
E
pillar large brown deteriorating~
   The pillar looks very old, in fact you can watch it crumble as small pieces
of it roll down out of cracks in it's side.  It has deteriorated so much that
there is a large pile of tiny pieces of it lying around the base.  It is about
seven feet tall, and standing about five feet from the treeline it is dwarfed
by the giant trees, but is still an impressive as an object made by man.  At
first the color of the pillar seems almost brown, but when you look closer you
can tell it was once a very bright white.  You wonder what material it was made
of, given the surroundings you realize someone would have had to bring the rock
from a far away place, and that just makes you wonder about who or what made it
and why.    
~
S
#1108
A Large Clear Area~
   Taking a look around the area you take in everything you see, which sadly,
doesn't seem to be very much at all.  The ground here is covered with a dark
green moss-like plant, in a few areas the moss has allowed small clumps of some
odd looking grass to grow.  The grass is a brown sort of color, but does not
appear to be dying, and a closer look reveals extremely small pink flowers
growing on the underside of each blade of the grass, a very odd plant indeed!
Aside from this odd grass and the moss, there is absolutely nothing to see,
only that about five feet from where you are standing, you see a forest line,
though there are no large trees or even saplings grow outside this very
definite line.  Oh well, for now you suppose you'll just have to continue on
walking, the clearing is cut out in north and south directions, with a trail to
your east.    
~
