#1113
A Small Trail at the Base of a Small Hill~
   The ground here is made of dirt, and is void of all grass or other type of
plantlife, though moss does grow around the trail, about six inches out from
the center of this small trail.  Making a tight circle around the base of the
hill here, the trail doesn't seem to serve any purpose whatsoever.  You could
walk along the trail to get a good look at the back of the entrance on this
small hill here, but that is about it.  Getting down and taking a close look at
the trail, you make out the tops of many large stepping stones that have been
buried under a small amount of ground here to make the trail what it is.  
After taking everything you see in, you have to wonder about what you see, all
these work out here in the middle of nowhere.  The trail you are on travels
both east and west from this point, the west continuing around the hill, and
the east going off to a curve.    
~
