E
slab writing lines carving~
   The slab is a flat piece of the same pale stone the pillars are made of,
lying face down in the dirt and tilted against a stump of rock.  Working your
boot under its edge, you roll it far enough to see the underside: it is
covered with lines of that angular writing, neat as a ledger, every mark cut
deep and then filled with some black stuff that has never washed out.
~
