#1129
Inside the Western Entrance~
   Looking around you realize that this place would make an excellent storm
shelter, as the walls and ceiling are made of huge slabs of some odd white
stone.  Covering the stone you see millions of extremely small mushrooms,
growing out of every small chip and crack.  They appear to be slightly glowing
in the darkness, but not quite enough to be very useful.  While examining the
stone walls you notice that the wall seperating this room from the eastern
entrance only goes part of the way, so you can see that the rooms merge into
one single hallway to the north.  While looking to the south you are slightly
distracted by a larger fungus formation growing, but the exit to the outside is
obvious.    
