#1133
The Firefly Room~
   As you look around the room, hundreds of tiny little almost translucent
little flies light up the room.  Each of the little fireflies are too small to
even touch, in fact that almost seem to go through you.  They fly in this room
only, none leaving to go anywhere else.  The fireflies are very interesting
creatures, they are here, but yet not, when you try to grasp them they go right
through you as if they were just small bits of light.  A blue skin seems to
cover the walls in this cave, you aren't sure what type of mineral or fungus it
is that grows, but you find it interesting how so many forms of life grow in
this cave.  To the north this hallway stretches even further into this odd cave
with block lined walls, and to the west you so a corner room where the hallway
bends.    
