#1141
The Entrance Hallway~
   Looking around the area you notice that this hallway room is a very dark
place indeed.  The walls in this room are made of a cold, dark grey stone that
has been cut into medium sized blocks about seven inches high by two feet wide.
Grating is the floor here, made of some sort of metal woven into a thick mesh
wire.  Looking through the gaps in it, you can see that they have been set
about two feet above the natural ground, providing plenty of room for liquids
to drain off.  At one time there must have been many beings working down in
this odd place, and the grating was probably made to keep disease and bacterial
growth down, but that's just an idea.  Looking for exits, you see to the west
that there is more of this strange hallway leading further into the cave, and
to the south you see a room with steps ending in it.    
