bricks that are made of a cut stone.  By the looks of them, the cutter didn't
do a very good job, as they are all very rough.  Grating is the floor, set up
about two feet from the natural ground, it allows for liquids to drain out and
exit out, probably to some underground river or something.  Looking up the
walls, you notice about six feet up, that there are large rings with locks
hooked on to them, hanging about three or four feet apart.  You aren't real
sure what they're for, but right now you look for the exits.  To the north the
hallway goes out into a large opening, but you can't really tell what's there.
