#1145
A Connector Room~
   Looking around the room, you realize it's just a connecting hallway room.  
The walls and ceiling are both made of a roughly cut stone, probably the
cheapest thing available for use in a dungeon.  The room is only barely lit,
this makes seeing anything very hard, but there are so many bugs it looks like
the walls are moving.  You are startled when you see a very large bug creeping
across the grating on the floor, but then realize it's just a shadow from a
tiny roach.  To the north is more of this hallway, connecting the rest of this
underground dungeon together, but to both the east and west are interconnecting
cells.    
~
