#1146
The Western Cell Block~
   The western section of the cell blocks appears to have many more nicer cells
than the rest of the dungeon has.  This section of the dungeon must have been
not been for murders, rapists, or common thieves, but instead it was probably
reserved for political prisoners or for interrogation.  The walls are made of a
smooth marble material that is almost soothing to look at, you find it very odd
for it to be used as a cell wall in an underground dungeon.  Even the floors
here have been kept up better than the rest, made of an entirely different
material and in a strange style.  The cells continue to go to the west, but
there is an exit out into the main section of the dungeon to the east.  Both of
the exits are beyond cell doors.    
~
