#1148
A Small Room~
   You are in a small bare room.  It would appear that this room was created
not as a prison cell, but instead it looks as if it was used as maybe a guard's
quarters so that if there was an emergency in a cell, someone could be deployed
from different parts of the dungeons.  Though, if this really was used as a
room for guards, you can't see who would want to through the hassles of going
through all those cells just to get to his or her quarters here, but then, this
is a very good room, and for all you know they could have stayed in here for a
week or more per shift.  If that was the case, it must have been a rough job,
or possibly one given to former prisoners themselves, because it would seem
being locked in this room for so long would get one feeling they too were
jailed.  The only way out of this small room, is a cell door to the south, made
just like all the other cell doors, giving you the feel that you've been
imprisoned.    
~
