ledger sheets writing ink book~
   The ledger is a bound stack of thin grey sheets, and the hand in it is the
same angular writing that is cut into the stones of this place, done here
with a brush and some brown ink gone the colour of old blood.  The last page
that was filled stops in the middle of a line, as if the writer meant to come
back to it, and every page after is blank.
~
E
keys ring iron peg~
   An iron ring hangs from a peg set into the wall, meant to carry the keys
of this level.  It is all but empty: a single worn stub of a key is left on
it, and pressed into the dust of the shelf beneath are the clean circles
where a great weight of iron used to lie.  Whoever went out of this room last
went out with every key but that one.
~
