lines writing marks script~
   You follow the lowest line of the writing with your eye until it trails
off into a stutter of single marks a hand's width above the floor.  Under it,
pressed into the dust, lies a small dark heap of bones, and they are far too
slight to have belonged to any keeper of this place.
~
S
#1164
The Washroom~
   A row of stone basins runs the length of the north wall, each worn smooth
in a ring where many hands have rested, and a channel carries what was tipped
from them to a grating in the floor.  The channel is dry, but the stain of
the water is still to be seen on every basin.
~
