hollow bowl stain block~
   The stain is not soot.  It has gone into the stone itself, a grey-black
that no scraping will touch, thickest at the bottom of the hollow and thinning
toward the rim in the way of a thing that was poured in and burned.  The
white stone about it is cold, colder than the room.
~
